      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PENNY BLACK NZ (1) is in good form and deserves a win after placing in her last four outings. Drew wider and did some work but stuck on for third last week. The ace draw gives her every chance to break through. Former Kiwi WE WALK BY FAITH (9) made an impressive start in WA when he came from a 50m handicap and raced three wide without cover but proved too good. Tackles a stronger bunch and draws widest but he is a talent. HARRISON JOHN NZ (3) put the writing on the wall when he drew on the back row and raced three wide without cover but fought well to miss narrowly last week. Should be at his peak for this and is much better served by this barrier. SWEET PINS NZ (6) was held up last time but recorded a series of top-three results prior including a Listed win two back so is worth including.",
